WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.602
Before you write any pivot query, complete one sentence: one output row represents what?

00:00:07.602 --> 00:00:12.992
Once that is clear, decide which categories should become columns.

00:00:12.992 --> 00:00:17.675
Then decide which value or measure should fill those columns.

00:00:18.147 --> 00:00:24.154
Finally, ask whether more than one source row can contribute to the same output cell.

00:00:24.154 --> 00:00:31.980
If the answer is yes, you need an aggregation rule such as sum, count, maximum, or average.
